<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joan III, Countess of Burgundy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1308–<a href="/years/1347">1347</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joan III was countess of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> (the Franche-Comté) and of Artois from 1330 until her death in 1347, the eldest daughter of King Philip V of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. In 1318 she married Duke Odo IV of Burgundy, uniting the duchy and the Free County of Burgundy under one ruling couple. Their grandson Philip I inherited both, but his death in 1361 ended the Capetian dukes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joan-iii-countess-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="Joan III, Countess of Burgundy" width="240" height="207" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Louis DESCHAMPS DE PAS · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jeanne2France.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
